{
  "requirement": "`habeas_sdk::graph` MUST define `Snapshot` as follows:\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n```\n\nFor node reads, the SDK MUST construct the snapshot by calling\n`Fingerprinting::fingerprint` with the node identity and contents returned by `Graph::node_content`, without\nreading the node again to compute its fingerprint. Graph operations returning\nsnapshots directly MUST supply fingerprints of the results from those same\nobservations. The SDK MUST NOT require `T` to carry a filesystem path or source\nspan.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.graph.fingerprinting.snapshot`. I did not run them. I mapped each clause to the tests as follows.\n\n**Definition of `Snapshot`** (`pub content`, `pub fingerprint`, `Clone`, `Debug`).\n- This is a declarative type. The derive attributes have no conditionals or transformation, so they need no test of their own.\n- External test crates build `Snapshot { content, fingerprint }` directly. `GraphWithChangingEdges::outgoing_edges` in `tests/agent.rs` does this, which exercises the public fields.\n- `Clone` is exercised by the retained-edge path in `prepare_edges`. The traversal and agent tests reach that path.\n\n**Node reads: fingerprint is built from `Fingerprinting::fingerprint`, the node identity and the contents returned by `node_content`, with no second read.**\n- `tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_node_snapshot]` reads a snapshot with `read_snapshot`, then mutates the graph.\n  - It asserts that the snapshot fingerprint equals the one computed from the supplied content (\"1:before\"), not from the mutated \"after\" state.\n  - It asserts that fingerprinting the same content under `Node(2)` differs, so the node identity is passed through.\n- `tests/validation.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts `reads == [1,1,1,2]`. That is exactly one `node_content` call per read, so there is no extra read to compute the fingerprint.\n  - It also checks that the recorded dependencies carry the fingerprints of what was actually read (\"before\" and \"after\" as separate entries).\n- `tests/agent.rs#fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` checks that recorded `Dependency::Node` fingerprints equal the content that was delivered. That covers the `prepare_read` path.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` fingerprints retained content separately from current content with the real `HabeasDomain`. Fingerprinting the retained content stays stable after the source changes, and fingerprinting the new content differs.\n\n**Operations returning snapshots directly supply fingerprints from the same observation.**\n- `tests/agent.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_use_traversals_retained_selection_without_relisting]` has a graph that errors on a second `outgoing_edges` lookup. It asserts exactly one lookup and that the recorded `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` carries the originally returned fingerprint (\"retained 1\"). The fingerprint is therefore the one from the observation that was delivered, not a re-listing.\n- `tests/validation.rs#fn[traversal_keeps_discovered_edges_and_reuse_does_not_skip_children]` checks that the recorded dependency fingerprint is the one from the discovered edges.\n- `tests/validation.rs#fn[labeled_selection_records_all_edges_without_reading_targets]` checks that the edge-list fingerprint changes under edge mutation, reordering and removal, and that no node content is read.\n- `tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` checks the recorded edge and node dependency fingerprints.\n\n**`T` need not carry a path or span.** The tests instantiate `Snapshot<String>`, `Snapshot<Vec<Edge<..>>>` and the `u8`/`HabeasNode` domains, none of which carries a path or span. A requirement that `T` carry one would fail to compile.\n\nI found no unmarked relevant tests, no gaps, and no acknowledgments to check.",
  "references": "3f42012c7c93776ac767bee25e175bbe42c19128953d6494c28fe1b0ab013b9a",
